Z||000000||4BanGinFun||12-07-2001||11:38 PM||||yup the time has come i need more power and torq but the cash is a problem  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> and cheap mods or adjustments???? <P>------------------<BR>85 se 2m4 5spd white<P><BR>www.angelfire.com/super/camaro0/||||reg||5
Z||000001||ITB 2M4||12-08-2001||12:58 AM||||Porting the head would probably be the biggest gain in power for cheap.  It will only cost you the price of a porting tool.  You could find someone to do it for you if you've never done it.  You don't want to go too far when you port, cause it's not easy to repair a hole in the intake runner.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4<BR>AOL IM- DGPFiero||||reg||10
Z||000002||AusFiero||12-08-2001||02:41 AM||||I thought stickers and a 3 inch tail pipe  was the cheapest mods around  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>But seriously. For not a lot of bucks start with the intake and exhaust.<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero3.gif">       <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000003||fierospeeder||12-08-2001||04:04 AM||||advance the timing, but you might have to increase the octane that you buy.<P>if you were dragracing, you would increase every 2degrees, until you didn't gain.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||12-08-2001||10:13 AM||||Lets say your cheap mods increase your horsepower by 10%.  For the 2.5L duke with 92hp to start with, the increase is 9 hp.<P>Do you think you will notice any real improvement?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Master_Sushi||12-08-2001||11:02 AM||||You'll probably notice a big diff between 92hp and 101hp.||||reg||1
Z||000006||turbo86se||12-08-2001||11:02 AM||||Best things I did for my first Fiero, a '85 coupe, not cheap, but not expensive:<BR>1. Hi-flow cat $110<BR>2. Flowmaster muffler $70<BR>3. Ultimate dogbone $50<P>With the exhaust, it ran much better, opened it up a bit. Sounded very good too! <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SC.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Mach10||12-08-2001||12:40 PM||||Cheapest mod? Get out and push!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Sorry, I'm shootin' my mouth off again, aren't I? :P<P>||||reg||10
Z||000008||fotofrank||12-08-2001||03:01 PM||||My '85 Duke has at least 104HP. I added (but not cheap): MSD6A, MSD GM Blaster coil, K&N filter, Holley TB, Holley intake (one for sale on the forum), Hooker header, hi flow cat. P.S.mine is an auto and I do notice the differance. For best results with my set-up do not use platinum plugs or split fires.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE||||reg||10
Z||000009||qwikgta||12-08-2001||05:45 PM||||I added a hooker header with open exhaust, no cat, to a supertrapp muffler.  I also added a open element air cleaner that I made by using the stock air cleaner base, cut off 1/4 inch from bottom, with a K&N filter and chrome lid.  I also have an ultimate bone and short shifter, new master and slave cly.  I have no idea on HP or TQE but I did notice a diff in the 1-2 and 2-3 shifts soon after the mods.  I will soon be adding a ported and polished intake and maybe a cam this winter.  <P>Rob   <P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/engine2_4.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/engine1_6.jpg"> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||4BanGinFun||12-08-2001||05:50 PM||||i was thinkin of getting a k&n filter i herd that they give anywhere from 10 - 20 hp  <P>would a daul outlet muffler add anything?? <BR>i was concidering the holly tb <P>stickers and a fart can hummmm i'll have to try it    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> a coffee can should do eh??    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>qwikgta looks good me want <P><BR>------------------<BR>85 se 2m4 5spd white<P> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/super/camaro0/" TARGET=_blank>www.angelfire.com/super/camaro0/</A> <P>[This message has been edited by 4BanGinFun (edited 12-08-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by 4BanGinFun (edited 12-08-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000011||MR2KLR||12-08-2001||09:32 PM||||A dual outlet muffler will not flow as well as a single outlet muffler. A I ran a straight pipe on my 84 and you can feel it rev quicker and it will have more top end at the cost of low end.  <P>160° thermostat<BR>Straight pipe (not emissions legal though)<BR>Punch out the air silencer in the rear 1/4<BR>K&N Filter<BR>free flow muffler<BR>advance the timing a few °<BR>Port the exhaust manifold<BR>Install a nickle (5¢) in the fuel pressure regulator 84-86 (will boost pressure)<P>or if you want to spend a bit more to get more<P>Deck the head & port it<P>big block chevy 1.6-1.7 ratio roller rockers ( I'll split a set with you E-mail me anyone)<P>if you can find one get a Holley dominator intake manifold (saw one in the mall yesterday $180<P>and a Cam to top it all off<P>if you just start off easy as you get the $$$ before you know it you'll be able to keep up with a stock GT.<P>------------------<BR>  <BR>Black 88 Coupe: 120 MPH spedo, Aux. gauge pod, 195/55VR14 Potenza RE-71 tires, GT exhaust & ground F/X Soon to have 16" White Beretta GTZ W/ 215/45ZR16's<BR><A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOY/" TARGET=_blank>Tom's Page</A>||||reg||1
