Z||000017||Blacktree||12-11-2001||01:51 AM||||The cheapest "useful" mod I ever did to my '86 4-banger Fiero was to cut out the catalytic converter and replace it with a straight piece of pipe (replacing the stock exhaust manifold with a Hooker header should help a bit, too). Luckily, I live in a state that doesn't have emissions tests, or the open exhaust would get me in trouble. <P>That combined with a glass-pack muffler and a K&N air filter resulted in a noticeable performance increase. I'm not sure of the actual numbers, but the car seemed to have better throttle response and slightly better acceleration.<P>Advancing the timing a few degrees and running 93 octane gasoline helped, also.<p>[This message has been edited by Blacktree (edited 12-11-2001).]||||reg||1
